Depends: claw-os-base (= __VERSION__), chromium, libnss3, libxss1, libasound2, libatk1.0-0, libatk-bridge2.0-0, libcups2, libdrm2, libdbus-1-3, libxcomposite1, libxdamage1, libxfixes3, libxrandr2, libgbm1, libpango-1.0-0, libcairo2, fonts-liberation, xdg-utils
Description: Claw OS — cos-browser engine (vendored Obscura)
 The cos-browser engine drives a headless Chromium via the Chrome
 DevTools Protocol, exposing it as `cos app web` and `cos browser`
 subcommands. This package installs the `cos-browser` and
 `cos-browser-worker` binaries.
 .
 The CDP server (`cos-browser serve --port 9222`) is opt-in via the
 systemd unit shipped in `claw-os-systemd`. Install both packages and
 `systemctl enable --now cos-browser.service` to expose an authenticated
 loopback CDP endpoint at boot.
